        "date": "2026-11-14T12:32:56Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Carvera states the clearance Z before the first X/Y traverse after M6\n\nThe Carvera post wrote a bare G0 X Y right after M6 T, at the height the\nchanger left the spindle. The open firmware source (ATCHandler.cpp,\non_main_loop) shows that M6 ends at machine Z clearance_z over the X/Y\nwhere the spindle was before the change, not over the tool rack. So the\nCarvera now writes G0 Z<ClearancePlane|RetractPlane> first after M6 too,\nthe same as at a program start. The changedAt branch is removed.\n\nPinned by the_carvera_states_the_clearance_before_any_xy_after_its_m6 and\nthe_carvera_script_cites_where_its_m6_leaves_the_spindle. The 19 Carvera\nNC goldens are not regenerated here; the maintainer decides.\n\nFixes #1616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
